Dear Mr Mitul Jain,
3rd Edition
IGBC's Green Gujarat Summit 2026
Friday | 12 June 2026 | Hotel Le Meridien, Ahmedabad
Parallel Session
Accelerating the Acceptance of Low-Carbon Cement
Advancing Sustainable Construction through Low-Carbon Materials
Time: 11:00 AM - 1:30 PM
We are pleased to share that the Indian Green Building Council (IGBC), a pa=
rt of the Confederation of Indian Industry (CII), has been at the forefront=
 of promoting sustainable and green building practices in India since 2001.=
 With over 15.90 billion sq. ft. of registered green building footprint and=
 19,330+ projects adopting IGBC's green building rating systems, India toda=
y stands among the top two countries globally in terms of registered green =
building footprint.
As part of the 3rd Edition of IGBC's Green Gujarat Summit 2026, we are orga=
nizing a focused parallel session on "Accelerating the Acceptance of Low-Ca=
rbon Cement: Advancing Sustainable Construction through Low-Carbon Material=
s."
[cid:image001.jpg@01DCF445.36D8F060]

The construction sector is one of the largest contributors to global carbon=
 emissions, with cement production accounting for a significant share. As I=
ndia advances toward its Net Zero commitments, the adoption of low-carbon c=
onstruction materials is becoming increasingly critical. This session aims =
to bring together industry leaders, developers, architects, policymakers, c=
onsultants, researchers, and material manufacturers to discuss practical pa=
thways for accelerating the adoption of low-carbon cement and reducing embo=
died carbon in the built environment.
Key Discussion Areas
* Embodied Carbon vs Operational Carbon
* Transition to Low-Carbon Cement
* Challenges in Adoption and Market Acceptance
* Industry Case Studies and Success Stories
* Sustainable Construction Pathways for Net Zero Buildings
Who Should Attend
* Construction & Infrastructure Companies
* Architects & Consultants
* Developers & Contractors
* Ready-Mix Concrete (RMC) Producers
* Policymakers & Government Representatives
* Sustainability Professionals
* Academia & Researchers
Objective of the Session
* Promote awareness and adoption of low-carbon cement technologies
* Explore strategies for reducing embodied carbon in construction projects
* Share successful implementation experiences and industry best practices
* Foster collaboration between industry, academia, and policymakers
* Support India's transition towards sustainable and Net Zero construction
This session will serve as a valuable platform for knowledge exchange, inno=
vation, and collaboration, helping stakeholders identify practical solution=
s for decarbonizing the construction sector and advancing climate-resilient=
 development.
With this, I would request you to kindly block your diary and join us for t=
his insightful session during the 3rd Edition of IGBC's Green Gujarat Summi=
t 2026, scheduled on 12 June 2026 at Hotel Le Meridien, Ahmedabad, from 11:=
00 AM to 1:30 PM.
For Registration, kindly click on the link below:
https://forms.mycii.in/form/7fb1f125-d53d-4c7d-90cd-badb770506f4
We at IGBC look forward to your participation and support in driving materi=
al innovation, climate action, and the Net Zero transition in the built env=
ironment.
For sponsorship opportunities or any queries, please contact Mr. Aditya She=
khar, Associate Counsellor, CII-IGBC | M: +91 93271 42820 | E: aditya.shekh=
ar@cii.in.
Regards,
Taral Shah
Chairman, IGBC Ahmedabad Chapter & MD, Shivalik Group
Shaan Zaveri
Co-Chair, IGBC Ahmedabad Chapter & Partner, Collated Ventures


